# A RIGHT PROGRAM (after two servers). In front of a loop with quiet turns there are two rows of blocks, and each operation that is built in front is sent to its row. Where proofs are
# checked at run time (testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime, which --aot-harden=proof-checks stands for) a read of a slot has a test of its own whether the slot is filled. Built "where it stands", that test was not sent: it landed in the
# first row, and its operand, the Unbox of what the read in front of it gave, stands in the second: the build stopped: UseNotDominated. The sending carries nothing out of a turn: it only picks the row.
# RUN(BUILDS): run-in-shell testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime
# BUILDS: true 0 true 2 false 3 true 3 true 0 true 0
# BUILDS-NEXT: exited with 0
# BUILDS-NEXT: the source prints the same
